---
// Goal: say what thinkthen backends check sends, what each report row means, and when it exits 4.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
import { BACKENDS_SEE } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { TOOLS_SEE } from '../../data/reference.mjs';
import { captioned, run } from '../../data/samples.mjs';

const [probes] = captioned('reference/check', TOOLS_SEE.check);
const plan = run('install/backends/system-one', '4-check-plan');
const spec = 'https://github.com/botassembly/thinkthen/blob/main/specification/check.md';
const ROWS = ['connection', 'key', 'endpoint', 'noul', 'choice', 'score', 'mixed', 'usage'];
---
<Base title="backends check" description={'What thinkthen backends check sends, what each report row means, and when it exits 4.'}>
  <h1><code>backends check</code></h1>
  <p class="lede"><code>thinkthen backends check</code> tests whether a server works with ThinkThen. It sends four fixed requests, one after another. Every request is real. A hosted server may charge for it.</p>
  <p><code>thinkthen check</code> remains a hidden compatibility alias with the same options, requests, report and exit codes.</p>

  <h2 id="plan">See it first</h2>
  <p><code>--plan</code> prints the address and the model, then the four request bodies and a count. It sends nothing and needs no key.</p>
  <Terminal run={plan} caption={BACKENDS_SEE['system-one']['4-check-plan']} />

  <h2 id="probes">The four probes</h2>
  <p>Each probe asks about the same parcel delivery, and each covers the question shapes some functions send.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>noul</code>: a yes or no question, for <code>decide</code>, <code>filter</code>, <code>rank</code>, and the yes or no questions of <code>recognize</code> and <code>relate</code>.</li>
    <li><code>choice</code>: a pick, for <code>choose</code>, <code>find</code>, and the kind question of <code>recognize</code>.</li>
    <li><code>score</code>: a scale, for <code>score</code>.</li>
    <li><code>mixed</code>: five questions of three kinds in one request, for <code>tag</code>, <code>annotate</code>, and any request that carries many questions.</li>
  </ul>
  <Terminal run={probes} caption={probes.see} />

  <h2 id="the-report">The report</h2>
  <p>A live check prints one <code>reply</code> line for each probe it decoded, then eight rows in this order: {ROWS.map((r, i) => <>{i ? (i === ROWS.length - 1 ? ' and ' : ', ') : ''}<code>{r}</code></>)}. A row reads <code>ok</code>, <code>warning</code> or <code>critical</code>. It reads <code>unchecked</code> when the check stopped before reaching it. A last line counts the critical and warning lines.</p>
  <p>A transport failure, or status 401, 402, 403 or 404, stops the check, because every later request would meet it too. Any other failure belongs to its probe, and the check goes on. A finding never quotes the reply.</p>

  <h2 id="exit-codes">Exit codes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>0: no row is critical. Warnings may stand.</li>
    <li>2: a usage error, such as no address or an unknown option. Nothing is sent.</li>
    <li>4: a row is critical, or the key is unset at an address other than this machine.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><code>backends check</code> reads no input, cache, recording or profile. <code>--cache</code>, <code>--no-cache</code>, <code>--record</code>, <code>--replay</code> and <code>--profile</code> are refused at exit 2. It takes no <code>--max-retries</code>, and four probes send at most sixteen attempts.</p>

  <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
  <p>A check has no fixed worst case. A server's <code>Retry-After</code> or <code>Retry-After-Ms</code> header sets a minimum wait before a retry, with no cap. Without either header, a check at <code>--timeout 90</code> takes about 25 minutes at most.</p>
  <p><code>THINKTHEN_MAX_ESTIMATED_INPUT_TOKENS_TOTAL</code> binds each probe. A probe the cap cannot admit stops the check before it is sent. The check prints no report and exits 2.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/install/backends/system-one/">Any System One server</a> · <a href={spec}>The check specification</a> · <a href="/learn/answers/#exit-codes">Every exit code</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The long variable name in prose wraps, so a phone does not scroll sideways. */
  p code { white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
